{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385358-what-do-you-think-the-canon-npcs-are-up-to","id":1385358,"title":"What do you think the canon NPCs are up to?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-02T23:12:57-07:00","id":1385358,"title":"What do you think the canon NPCs are up to?","content":"Basically another fanon thread. Here's where you get to tell us what canon NPCs (Theo Bell, Victoria Ash, Beckett) or so on are up to in your campaign world.<br /> <br /> There's countless wonderful and fascinating characters in V5 and while the ones in Chicago have been updated, there's still hundreds more that haven't been updated.<br /> <br /> Share what they're doing in your games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T10:30:01-07:00","id":1385429,"title":"","content":"Some examples to start us off:<br /> <br /> + <b>Jan Pieterszoon</b> is actually not dead in my games but is in hiding because he believes Theo Bell was actually dominated by Lucinda into killing Hardestadt. He believes the &quot;Secret Masters&quot; of the Ventrue set up the end of the Camarilla and the exile of the Brujah. He has since altered his face, identity, and is living off the grid while he descends into paranoia. I'm actually debating that he stupidly went to Vykos who tortured him and deformed him before releasing him into Chicago as &quot;Olaf.&quot; Otherwise, he's living like Lestat at the end of Interview. Part of the issue is his Blood Bond to Hadestadt breaking and removal of years of Dominate has broken down his barriers against the guilt of his Feeding restriction.<br /> <br /> + <b>Lucita</b>'s brief reign as the Regent of the Sabbat was an unmittigated disaster as her attempts to institute badly needed reforms and purge the most insane resulted in a successful coup by Polonia. As such, she was part of the Amis Noctis that led to the defection of the Camarilla. She's also fallen away from the Path of Night and struggling to reconcile her indecision between it as well as Humanity. Lucita is looking for a new religion to help her stave off the beast but stubbornly refuses to turn to Anatole for spiritual advice. Talley actually helped her fake her death as she goes through this spiritual crisis.<br /> <br /> + <b>Jeremy MacNeil </b>was Beckoned to the Middle East so he's not going to be doing much anytime soon.<br /> <br /> +<b> Tyler</b> was Beckoned...and came back. Tyler has no memory of what happened but has been invigorated with visions of Carthage and its glories. She's also much-much more powerful than she used to be and is effectively able to casually toss aside any Elder she meets. She is now eliminating Camarilla and Sabbat elders while convincing others to aid in the Anarch's reformation. Her Anarchs are a violent philosopher-warrior cabal dedicated to the vision of their Mother, though.<br /> <br /> + <b>Hesha</b> turned out to be a big part of the early Ministry due to his encounter with Beckett's sarcophagus at the end of BJD. The discovery that the 2nd generation were real caused a severe crisis of faith and he's one of the ones who helped many of them defect to the Anarchs and embrace polytheism. He's furthermore become a part of the Church of Caine because its gnosticism is similar enough to the Setite orthodoxy that it's familiar but different in its origins. He knows his &quot;heresy&quot; would get him killed but he has a secret proector. He has since also become a national leader of the Anarchs if for no reason that he has a brain and can usually persuade a bunch of violent fanatics into following his lead (i.e. 80% of all Anarchs). The remaining 20% he can persuade through other means.<br /> <br /> + <b>The Ministry</b> is almost entirely the work of <b>Kemintiri</b> and she's their secret puppet master.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=